  "steps": [
    "For the chipotle dip - 150g fresh low fat paneer, 8-10 soaked cashews (soak in hot water for at least 1 hour), 2-3 spicy dry red chilies (soak in hot water for at least 1 hour), 1 cheese cube (optional), 2/3 tsp salt, 1 tsp oregano, 2/3 tsp kashmiri red chili powder, 1.5 tsp extra virgin olive oil, 2-3 ice cubes, 1/3 cup water (add as per requirement to adjust the consistency).",
    "Blend everything well until you get a smooth creamy texture as shown in the video!",
    "The dip is now ready, you can store this in an air tight container & refrigerate for upto 3 days.",
    "For the sandwich - bread slices. Apply a generous layer of the chipotle dip on both breads, top with veggies of choice (I have used onions, capsicum & tomato).",
    "Sprinkle a little chaat masala on the veggies, toast the sandwich in some ghee/olive oil until crispy & golden brown on both sides.",
    "Serve this with some more dip or tomato ketchup!"
  ],
